        -:   53:/**
        -:   54: * Represent a set of closed polygons. Polygons may be nonconvex, self-intersecting
        -:   55: * and have holes. Provides boolean operations (using Clipper library as the backend).
        -:   56: *
        -:   57: * Let us define the terms used on this class to clarify methods names and comments:
        -:   58: *      - Polygon: each polygon in the set.
        -:   59: *      - Outline: first polyline in each polygon; represents its outer contour.
        -:   60: *      - Hole: second and following polylines in the polygon.
        -:   61: *      - Contour: each polyline of each polygon in the set, whether or not it is an
        -:   62: *      outline or a hole.
        -:   63: *      - Vertex (or corner): each one of the points that define a contour.
        -:   64: *
        -:   65: * TODO: add convex partitioning & spatial index
        -:   66: */
        -:   67:class SHAPE_POLY_SET : public SHAPE
